extraction_notes: "WB20 Canada printed 116-120 (cache p117-p121, cache page = printed folio + 1), read off the text layer; no render was needed. The heading on printed 116 reads Headhunter Anti-Robot Specialist O.C.C.; the stat block on printed 119 is headed Anti-Robot Headhunters O.C.C. and the experience table names it Anti-Robot Headhunter; also printed as Robot Slammer. || GROUP: every Headhunter is called a die-hard man of arms (printed 109) and the class is listed under Headhunter O.C.C.s (printed 107); occ_group men-of-arms, men_of_arms true, no sdc_base printed. Not tagged evil: alignment any. || XP: the Anti-Robot Headhunter ladder from the Experience Tables, printed 192, as supplied from a render. || BONUSES stored: +2D6 S.D.C. as a pool bonus, +1D4 M.E., +1 P.P., +1 roll with impact, +2 save vs electrocution as saves.other. NOT stored as numbers, in special_abilities: impervious to Horror Factor from robots, cyborgs, power armor and mechanical looking opponents; -2 to save vs Horror Factor against magic and the supernatural; +2 initiative against robots and power armor only; the psychic Slammer lines; triple damage on a natural 18-20 Aimed Shot against robots; Maximum Performance. || SKILLS NEEDING CATALOG ROWS: Language: Techno-Can (86% +1% per level printed), Literacy: Techno-Can (stored 70/5, the Literacy: Other 30/5 plus the printed +40%), Fanatic Robophile (the Slammer prints 64% +3%; every other O.C.C. takes it at 50% +3% as a Technical related skill only, with no O.C.C. bonus and its other mechanical and electronics bonuses halved, printed 118) and Hotwire Robot Vehicles & Power Armor (50% +3%, this class only). The catalog Hot Wiring row is the Heroes Unlimited skill and is not the same thing. || SKILL READINGS: Speak Native Language prints 94% with no per-level, stored 94/0. Surveillance Systems is the catalog Surveillance row. Find Contraband (+10%) is the catalog row at 26+10 with the catalog per-level; this class does not get the Headhunter variant. Pilot: Robots & Power Armor is Robots & Power Armor at 56+20; Pilot: Robot Basic is Robot Combat: Basic; Robot Elite two of choice is a pick of two among the Robot Combat Elite rows. Hand to Hand: Expert, Martial Arts or Assassin (if evil) for one other skill, Jujitsu for two. The Fanatic Robophile +5% to Robot Electronics, Robot Mechanics, Weapon Systems and Computer Repair is conditional on those skills being taken and is in the related note. || RELATED: two at each of levels 1, 3, 6, 10 and 14. W.P. any but no specialized gunfighting skills from Rifts New West excludes W.P. Sharpshooting and W.P. Quick Draw. Secondary: four in total. || MONEY: 1D6x1000 credits (text layer !D6xlOOO) is starting_money; another 1D6x1000 in black market items is goods, in GM Notes. || EQUIPMENT: the fusion blocks print their own damage, 1D4x10 and 2D6x10 M.D. (text layer !D4xlO and 2D6xlO), matching the Triax catalog rows. High explosive hand grenades are stored on the Explosive Grenade row and Plasma grenades on the Plasma Grenade row. The text layer reads FDD pocket audio recorder/player; a render of printed 119 (cache p120) shows the page prints PDD, which is the catalog PDD pocket recorder row. The Universal Headjack & Ear Implant is stored as a row. NOT stored, no catalog row for Rifts: black paint stick, Automatic Lock Pick/Release Gun, lock pick kit, Electro-Adhesive Pads (the last three exist only as Heroes Unlimited rows), street clothes (two sets), box of 100 disposable plastic gloves, Multi-Optic Eye implant. Also not stored: one weapon per W.P. with three reloads, the suit of light or medium environmental armor, the two implants of choice, personal items. The Mode of Transportation percentile table is in special_abilities."
